‎## 7. Principle Reinforced
‎
‎**From Dispatch 012:**
‎> Tools evolve. Ecosystems evolve. Inhabitants evolve. But the capacity to issue a meaningful command remains.
‎
‎**Reinforced by Dispatch 013:**
‎> Coding doesn't get easier. Human capability relocates. The scarce resource moves from production to judgment.
‎
‎**For Knowledge Quest:**
‎The Knowledge Flywheel must be built for this relocation.
‎- Don't optimize for producing more LOGs (execution cheap)
‎- Optimize for judgment, architecture, verification, taste (scarce)
‎
‎This is [[KQ_LOG_2026-08-25]] — Inventory Before Intervention:
‎> Prove the flywheel moves reliably before adding resources.
‎
‎Because when execution becomes cheap, the flywheel that can *evaluate* and *compound* wins.
